    <fr:title text="Guarded Recursion and Linearity">Guarded Recursion and Linearity</fr:title>
    <fr:taxon>Daily</fr:taxon>
  </fr:frontmatter>
  <fr:mainmatter>
    <fr:p>In a discussion with Eric, we may have stumbled upon a neat interaction of guarded recursion and linearity.</fr:p>
    <fr:p>Could it be the case that guarded recursion in a linear setting would let you recover inductive reasoning? For instance, if I were to build a term of a guarded type in a finitary context, I could not do truly coinductive things. I will necessarily consume all of the input eventually or something like this.</fr:p>
  </fr:mainmatter>
